@page "/terms"
@inject TroopInfo Troop

@* Public: linked from every public page's footer and from the Google sign-in consent screen. *@

<PageTitle>Terms of Service - @Troop.AppName</PageTitle>

<article class="card legal">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: October 29, 2026</p>

    <p>These terms cover your use of @Troop.AppName (the "site", at @Troop.SiteHost). By
        signing in or using the site, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use the
        site.</p>

    <h2>Who runs the site</h2>
    <p>The site is run by volunteers of @Troop.Name, a Scouts BSA troop ("the troop", "we"). It is
        not operated or endorsed by Scouting America. Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        explains how we handle your information.</p>

    <h2>Who can use it</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Parents and guardians</strong> whose email address a troop leader has added.
            You sign in with a one-time code sent to that address.</li>
        <li><strong>Adult leaders</strong> whom a troop administrator has given access. You sign in
            with a Microsoft or Google account, and you can see or change only what your access
            level allows.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You must be at least 18 to use the site. Scouts do not have accounts.</p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>Keep your email account and any Microsoft or Google account you use secure, and don't share
        sign-in codes. You're responsible for what's done when you're signed in. Tell us right away
        at <a href="mailto:@Troop.ContactEmail">@Troop.ContactEmail</a> if you think someone
        else has used your access.</p>

    <h2>Reimbursements, invoices and payments</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Reimbursement requests must be for real troop expenses, with genuine receipts and
            accurate amounts. Whether a request is approved follows the troop's own policies and is
            up to the troop.</li>
        <li>The site keeps records only. It does not take or send money: payments happen outside
            the site, and a leader records them afterwards.</li>
        <li>We work to keep balances, invoices and records accurate, but mistakes can happen. If
            something looks wrong, contact the troop treasurer and we'll look into it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Adult leaders</h2>
    <p>If you have access to the admin area, use it only for troop business, keep families' and
        scouts' information confidential, and follow the troop's financial policies. Administrators
        may change or remove access at any time.</p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Don't misuse the site: no trying to reach information you haven't been given access to,
        interfering with how it works, uploading harmful files, or using it for anything unlawful.</p>

    <h2>Ending access</h2>
    <p>The troop may suspend or remove anyone's access, for example when a family leaves the troop
        or these terms aren't followed. Records may be kept as described in the Privacy Policy.</p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>The site is provided by volunteers "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any
        kind. We don't promise it will always be available or error-free.</p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>To the extent the law allows, the troop and its volunteers are not liable for indirect or
        consequential losses arising from use of the site, or for losses caused by circumstances
        beyond our reasonable control.</p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms. When we do, we'll change the date at the top of this page.
        Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:@Troop.ContactEmail">@Troop.ContactEmail</a>.</p>

    <p class="legal-links"><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> &middot; <a href="/">Back to @Troop.AppName</a></p>
</article>
